## 21. Ninth invocation (2026-09-11T18:16+08:00, ≈ X h): the pinned-operator finite existence theorem

### 21.1 Baseline re-verification

Every one of the 20 hashes recorded by the eighth invocation was re-computed with `sha256sum -c`
(`logs/d13_eighth_final_hashes.txt`: all OK, byte-identical), and the full suite was re-run on the
unchanged artifact before any write: `lake build` exit 0 (**9196 jobs**, D6AUDIT PASS,
`D13HeatKernelBridgeAxiomCheck` PASS **278/278**), semantic transcripts 8/8, per-file 17/17,
worktree 328/328, forbidden 0/0, negative control PASS, diff 6 expected new-file lines, upstream
snapshot PASS (`logs/d13_eighth_baseline_*`).

### 21.2 The gap and the repair

The fifth–eighth invocations proved, kernel-checked, that every universally quantified existence
statement over the schematic `HeatSpacetime` interface is **false as formalized** (the interface
leaves `laplacian`/`timeDerivative` free), and recorded the dependency: *an interface that pins the
operator to a genuine Laplace operator*. The ninth invocation constructs that interface in the
finite-dimensional setting and proves the existence theorem over it.

`FiniteHeatOperator X` (X finite) is a real matrix `L` with `Lᵀ = L`, `∑ y, L x y = 0` (constant
annihilation) and `0 < L x y` for `x ≠ y` (strictly positive off-diagonal entries). It is a genuine
discrete Laplace operator:

| property | declaration |
| --- | --- |
| constant annihilation `Δ 1 = 0` | `laplacian_one` |
| finite-level self-adjointness `∑ u·Δv = ∑ Δu·v` | `laplacian_selfAdjoint` |
| discrete Dirichlet identity `∑ u·Δu = -(1/2)∑∑ L (u x - u y)^2` | `laplacian_dirichlet_identity` |
| dissipativity / negative semidefiniteness `∑ u·Δu ≤ 0` | `laplacian_quadraticForm_nonpos` |
| nonzero when two points exist | `laplacian_ne_zero` |
| the class is nonempty (complete graph) | `completeGraphOperator` |

The heat kernel `finiteHeatKernel G x y t = (exp (t • L)) x y` (`t > 0`, clipped at `t ≤ 0`) is
proved to satisfy:

* strict positivity `0 < K x y t` for `t > 0` (shift trick `exp (t•L) = exp (-(t·c)) • exp (t•M)`
  with `M = L + c•1` entrywise positive, plus the single-term lower bound for the exponential
  series);
* symmetry, unit row sums and unit column sums;
* the entrywise bound `K x y t ≤ 1` (the Gaussian upper bound with `C_up = 1`, `dim = 0`,
  `dist = 0`);
* Chapman–Kolmogorov `K x y (s+t) = ∫ z, K x z s * K z y t` (counting measure);
* the genuine PDE `∂_t K(x,y,t) = Δ_x K(x,y,t)` as `HasDerivAt` (via
  `hasDerivAt_exp_smul_const'` and `hasDerivAt_pi`);
* the **full** Dirac initial condition against *all* functions (finite spaces have no continuity or
  integrability obstruction), hence both the legacy and the corrected quantifier;
* conservation of mass `∑ x, (e^{tL}u) x = ∑ x, u x`, the discrete parabolic **maximum principle**
  (positivity preservation) and the `ℓ¹`-contraction of the semigroup;
* non-degeneracy: strictly positive off-diagonal entries, so the kernel is not the degenerate
  identity kernel of `DataRefutation.lean`.

The interface-level consequences:

* `finiteHeatKernelCore` — the D11 core datum;
* `finiteHeatKernelData` — a **genuine legacy D7 `HeatKernelData`** with the full pointwise initial
  condition;
* `finiteHeatKernelDataV1` — the corrected-domain `HeatKernelDataV1`;
* `finiteHeatSpacetime` + `finiteHeatSpacetime_isClosedRiemannian` — the schematic spacetime is a
  closed Riemannian manifold (counting measure, discrete metric, compactness);
* `finite_isHeatKernelPDE` — inhabitation of the repaired predicate `IsHeatKernelPDE` (v2);
* `FinitePinnedHeatExistenceStatement` + `finitePinnedHeatExistenceStatement_proved` — the
  pinned-operator existence statement, **proved**;
* `finite_pinned_scope` — the conjunction with strict positivity, non-degeneracy and the nonzero
  constant-annihilating Laplacian.

